---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Brief = `Everyone votes for a lunch option and I have all the votes in
a list. Tell me which one won and how many votes it got. I do
not care about the rest of the tally.`;

const SampleOutput = `Votes: pizza, tacos, pizza, salad, pizza, tacos

Winner: pizza (3 votes)`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/unit-1/cc-set-4" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back to Set 4
        </a>

        <h1>Code Challenge: Most Common Value</h1>

        <p>
          <span class="badge text-bg-warning">Extra Credit</span>
          <span class="ms-2 text-body-secondary"
            >Not part of the five required for this set.</span
          >
        </p>

        <h4>
          Difficulty&nbsp;&nbsp;
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
        </h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="brief">
          <h2>The Brief</h2>

          <Code
            code={Brief}
            frame="code"
            lang="txt"
            title="What they asked for"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mt-3"
          />

          <p class="mt-4">
            <b>Write your requirements list before you write any code.</b> Input,
            calculate, output, and anything you had to decide for yourself. See{" "}
            <a href="/courses/ap-csp/unit-1/cc-set-4">Set 4</a> for what that looks like.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="notes">
          <h2>Notes</h2>

          <ul>
            <li>Start with the votes in an array of strings.</li>
            <li>You have no way to look something up quickly yet, so this needs a loop inside a loop: for each option, count how many times it appears.</li>
            <li>That is genuinely inefficient and it is the right answer at this stage. Note in your requirements list that you know it is doing more work than necessary.</li>
            <li>Decide what happens on a tie and say which you chose.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="sample-output">
          <h2>Sample Output</h2>

          <Code
            code={SampleOutput}
            frame="terminal"
            title="Sample Output"
            lang="txt"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mt-3"
          />

          <p class="mt-3">Nested loops over the same array is the technique here. If that feels clumsy, it is - and noticing that is worth as much as the working program.</p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Your requirements list and your program file, named{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-theme">cc-word-frequency</b>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <h1
          class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
        >
          Commence Challenge
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
